From a4bb6ab3a088d5146d8a61f5a2294948edbfbc3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 3dpdf <3dpdf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:27:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] UI/UX pass: fix zoom drift, add reset/screenshot/section

- Mouse-wheel zoom scaled the model around world origin, not around
  wherever the model currently is. Harmless before pan existed (the
  model rarely strayed far from origin), but after panning away zoom
  would visibly fly the model across the screen instead of growing/
  shrinking in place. Now scales around the model's own current
  translation.
- Added Home key / "Reset View" button (Camera tab): puts the camera
  and model back to their just-loaded state, needed now that pan/zoom
  can move the model somewhere the user can't easily undo by feel.
- Added F12 / "Save Screenshot" button (Main tab): saves the current
  frame to a timestamped PNG, reusing the same encode path batch mode
  (--output) already had.
- Added an always-on-screen control-hint caption (toggle: F1), so the
  mouse/key bindings are discoverable without opening the Debug panel.
- Added a "Section" tab: a world-space clipping plane (axis + offset +
  flip) that cuts away the model on one side, so you can see inside an
  enclosure without hiding individual parts one by one in the existing
  part-visibility tree. Implemented as a discard in the generic
  fragment shader, driven by new Scene/MeshShader plumbing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
